  "body": "**Blocked by:** none\n**Model tier:** low\n\n## Context\n\nModel tier rationale: This adds one missing row to an existing pure URL-validation rejection table.\n\n- PR #1158, finding `071e4c611f`, `backend/packages/data/src/__tests__/storedOutboundUrl.unit.test.ts:21`: The baseline helper rejection table tests localhost subdomains and root dots separately but omits their combined case already covered by the web-push validator.\n\n## Task\n\nAdd `https://api.localhost./x` to the rejection table for `isBaselineOutboundUrl`. Keep the current separate localhost, localhost-root-dot and localhost-subdomain cases, so the combined normalization/suffix condition is exercised directly. Run the baseline-helper and web-push validator unit suites without changing either validator.\n\n## Touches\n\n- backend/packages/data/src/__tests__/storedOutboundUrl.unit.test.ts (rejection table only)\n\n## Scope\n\n### In scope\n\nThe one omitted compound localhost case.\n\n### Out of scope\n\nURL policy changes, normalization changes, live network tests and expansion to other URL categories.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- For finding `071e4c611f`, the direct helper unit suite rejects `https://api.localhost./x` alongside the existing cases; the baseline-helper and web-push validator unit suites pass with production code unchanged.\n\n\n<!-- crb-followup:v1 pr=1158 key=071e4c611f -->",
